result.result:
Customer tiers are in. All 17 tests pass, including the new ones.

- **Cart:** `Cart` now has `tier`, defaulting to `"standard"` (`shop/models.py`).
- **Discount:** gold takes 10% off and silver 5%. Any other tier gets nothing (`shop/pricing.py`).
- **Tax:** the discount comes off the subtotal before tax is added. `calc_tax` taxes the discounted taxable amount, and `calc_total` is the discounted subtotal plus that tax. The tier discount stacks with the existing bulk discount.
- **Rounding:** each discount is rounded half up to the cent, using the existing `percent` helper.
- **Order:** it gets the discount through `calc_total` and `calc_tax`, and I also added an `order.tier` attribute (`shop/orders.py`). I did not add the tier to what `Store` saves.
- **CLI:** `quote --tier gold` (or any other value) works, defaulting to `standard` (`shop/cli.py`).

New tests are in `tests/test_pricing.py`, `tests/test_orders.py` and a new `tests/test_cli.py`. They cover:
- the default tier;
- gold and silver on taxable items;
- unknown tiers;
- gold on an untaxable item;
- stacking with the bulk discount;
- `Order` totals and tier;
- the `--tier` option end to end.
